1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,464
Two drafts almost went out under Harlan's name this section: a swelling claim nobody

2
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:09,117
had tested, and an avatar running on the wrong licence tier.

3
00:00:09,117 --> 00:00:10,092
Neither shipped.

4
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:14,962
Seven lectures ago, this section opened with a promise: catch the unshippable ad

5
00:00:14,962 --> 00:00:18,068
before it spends money or triggers a policy strike.

6
00:00:18,068 --> 00:00:19,529
Here's the honest tally.

7
00:00:19,529 --> 00:00:24,521
You now know the four ways an AI ad actually fails: an overreached claim, a rights

8
00:00:24,521 --> 00:00:27,261
gap, product drift, and a missing disclosure.

9
00:00:27,261 --> 00:00:32,193
You've seen two of those categories catch something real on Harlan's own account,

10
00:00:32,193 --> 00:00:36,637
the claim and the licence-tier gap, both killed before a dollar of spend.

11
00:00:36,637 --> 00:00:41,630
You know disclosure moved this year from a platform courtesy toward actual law, in

12
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:42,848
more than one place.

13
00:00:42,848 --> 00:00:47,962
And you've built B05, the checklist that runs all four checks with a named owner and

14
00:00:47,962 --> 00:00:52,894
a real checkpoint, not a list you have to reconstruct from memory under pressure.

15
00:00:52,894 --> 00:00:56,486
That's not a section about being cautious for its own sake.

16
00:00:56,486 --> 00:01:01,539
It's the difference between a batch that's fast to make and a batch that's actually

17
00:01:01,539 --> 00:01:03,549
safe to spend real money testing.

18
00:01:04,099 --> 00:01:09,154
Section seven is where everything from Sections two through six actually earns its

19
00:01:09,154 --> 00:01:14,333
keep: a batch, briefed properly, generated at volume, checked for every way it could

20
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:19,204
fail, and now ready for the one thing that actually tells you which angle wins.

21
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:21,115
Nothing gets rebuilt from here.

22
00:01:21,115 --> 00:01:22,040
It gets tested.
